      {
        "body": "Gain 4, Work 2, Harm 4\nRaise: Not done\nA blocked `forge close` publishes its review result before waiting for CI, so that result can be the last timestamp in the record. If it contains enough findings to exceed `RECORD_BUDGET`, `_compact` eventually has no later timestamp to use as a cut and breaks while the record is still oversized. At GitHub's body limit, `_bounded_body` can delete that result, losing the latest review evidence for a fresh clone. The fixed size requirement is therefore unmet for a large latest review.",
        "file": "src/forge/time_records.py",
        "gain": 4,
        "harm": 4,
        "line": 540,
        "priority": "P1",
        "title": "Not done: A large latest review escapes the fixed time record limit",
        "work": 2
      },
